      "content": "• Article 368 deals with the amendment procedure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e54rozr",
      "content": "• Article 356 relates to President's Rule in states."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 17 (Abolition of Untouchability) and Article 21A (Right to Education) are extremely high-frequency questions in SSC CGL, CHSL, and UPSC exams.",
        "Distinguish clearly between National Emergency (Article 352), President's Rule / State Emergency (Article 356), and Financial Emergency (Article 360).",
        "Writs under Article 32 can be issued only by the Supreme Court, whereas Article 226 empowers High Courts to issue writs for Fundamental Rights and other legal rights."
      ],
      "id": "b364vhq"
    },
